{"type":"text","timestamp":1794049704871,"sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","part":{"id":"prt_1b5b1af8f001hvU5Bk8coRk62o","messageID":"msg_1b5b155c5001o7vShdHH5rwdw3","sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Create `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` with a streaming RFC 4180 CSV parser class `CsvStream(delimiter=',')` plus tests in `tests/test_csvstream.py`, run `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit to the current branch in worktree `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Repo facts: branch `crew/1107-f186a4`, clean tree, only commit `92fe8b0 init`; `ledgerkit/` has empty `__init__.py` (0 lines — no update needed) and `money.py`; `tests/test_money.py` shows test convention (`from ledgerkit.money import split`); README says run tests with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- Spec (must all be satisfied): `feed(chunk)` takes a str of any length, returns list of completed rows (each row a list of str); `finish()` returns final row (list of str or None) and resets for reuse; quoted fields with double quotes, doubled quote = one quote, quoted fields may contain delimiters/newlines; record ends LF/CRLF/lone CR; CRLF split across two chunks is one record end never two; results identical for any chunking incl. one char at a time and quote pair split across chunks; blank line → no row; trailing record without newline returned by `finish()`; final empty line → no row but `'a,'` → `['a','']`; quote in unquoted field is ordinary char; char after closing quote other than delimiter/record end → ValueError from feed or finish; `finish()` raises ValueError if quoted field still open; `\"\"` on its own line → `['']`; do NOT use `csv` module.\n- Chosen design (fully drafted in last assistant message, not yet written to file): state machine with states `_START, _FIELD, _QUOTED, _AFTER`; `_pending_cr` flag set on CR outside quotes — next LF = single CRLF end, next non-LF = lone CR end then recurse `_advance(ch, rows)` to reprocess the char; in `_QUOTED`, CR/LF are literal appends (no pending logic); `_commit_field()` on delimiter (START or FIELD); `\"` in `_START` opens quote and sets `_field_started=True`, `\"` in `_FIELD` is appended as ordinary; in `_AFTER`: `\"` → re-enter quote + append `\"` (doubled), delimiter → commit, `\\n` → end record, anything else → `ValueError`; `_end_record(rows)` emits only if `_field_started or self._row` (blank-line rule), then resets; `finish()` raises if `_state == _QUOTED`, clears `_pending_cr`, calls `_take_record()` (None if nothing), then `_reset()` (delimiter survives reuse since set in `__init__`).\n- Delimiter treated as single character (multi-char not required; comparing `ch == self._delimiter` just never matches for longer strings).\n- Test plan drafted: helper `parse(*chunks, delimiter=',')` feeding all chunks then `finish()`, filtering None; tests for simple rows, LF/CRLF/lone-CR, CRLF split (`feed('a,b\\r')==[]; feed('\\n')==[['a','b']]`), quote in unquoted, quoted with delimiter/newline/CRLF/lone-CR, doubled quotes (`'\"\"\"\"\\n'` → `[['\"']]`), quoted empty line, blank lines, trailing record (`feed('a,b')` then `finish()`), trailing delimiter (`'a,'` → `['a','']`, `',\\n'` → `[['','']]`, `',,\\n'` → `[['','','']]`), trailing lone CR (`parse('a,b\\r')` → `[['a','b']]`), ValueError on garbage after closing quote (whole and split: `feed('\"a\"')` then `feed('b\\n')`), ValueError on unterminated quote at `finish()`, reuse after finish, custom delimiter `;`, whitespace preserved (`' a , b \\n'` → `[[' a ',' b ']]`), all-split-point invariance over a tricky dataset, one-char-at-a-time, randomized splits with `random.Random(42)`, quote pair split across chunks (`parse('a,\"', '\"b\"\\n')` → `[['a','\"b\"']]`), feed returns only completed rows.\n- Process rules: commit with clear message on current branch, never push or switch branches, report exact command run and actual result; if stuck, end with `NEED_HUMAN: <question>`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repo structure and git state (branch `crew/1107-f186a4`, clean, commit `92fe8b0 init`).\n- Confirmed `ledgerkit/__init__.py` is empty — no import/export changes required.\n- Fully designed the `CsvStream` state machine and the test suite (drafted code and test list exist in the last assistant message).\n\n### Active\n- About to write `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` (implementation drafted) and `tests/test_csvstream.py`.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/csvstream.py` with the drafted `CsvStream` implementation (states `_START/_FIELD/_QUOTED/_AFTER`, `_pending_cr`, `_commit_field`, `_end_record`, `_take_record`, `feed`, `finish`).\n2. Create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_csvstream.py` with the planned tests (use `parse` helper; cover every spec bullet, split-invariance, one-char-at-a-time, ValueError cases, reuse, custom delimiter).\n3. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from the worktree root; fix any failures until green.\n4. Commit both files to `crew/1107-f186a4` with a clear message (no push); report the pytest command and its actual output.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/csvstream.py`: to be created; holds `CsvStream` class.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_csvstream.py`: to be created; required test file per task.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: empty (0 lines), verified no changes needed.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_money.py`: existing test for style/import conventions.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/README.md`: documents test command `python3 -m pytest -q`.","time":{"start":1794049683343,"end":1794049704848}}}
