{"type":"text","timestamp":1794049769522,"sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","part":{"id":"prt_1b5b2dcb7001S5b4HKs4HYlsqJ","messageID":"msg_1b5b2101d001jZaN0LobTYdCi4","sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","type":"text","text":"\n\nThree failures, all from malformed test data, not parser bugs:\n\n1. `test_garbage_after_closing_quote_raises` — the parser (correctly) raises during `feed('\"a\" ')`, but my test expected it at `finish()`.\n2. `test_quote_pair_split_across_chunks` — `parse('a,\"', '\"b\"\\n')` concatenates to `a,\"\"b\"\\n`, which is malformed CSV (a doubled quote must be followed by a quote; it's followed by `b`). The parser correctly rejected it.\n3. `test_split_invariance_random_splits` — `\"t\"\"\\n...` never closes its quoted field (a field ending in a literal quote needs `\"t\"\"\"`).\n\nFixing the test data:\n\n\n\n","time":{"start":1794049760439,"end":1794049769519}}}
