{"type":"text","timestamp":1794049888352,"sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","part":{"id":"prt_1b5b48813001Y0khz6ps3qOmv3","messageID":"msg_1b5b4182d001VY7b62N9X1g0GR","sessionID":"ses_e4a523d64ffeZWJGrl6IZk2wti","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` with a streaming RFC 4180 CSV parser class `CsvStream(delimiter=',')`, add `tests/test_csvstream.py`, make `python3 -m pytest -q` pass, and commit on the current branch in worktree `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Worktree: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4`; branch `crew/1107-f186a4`; base commit `92fe8b0 init`; do not push or switch branches; report exact command and actual result.\n- `ledgerkit/__init__.py` is empty and does not need changes.\n- Parser constraints: no `csv` module; `feed(chunk)` accepts arbitrary string chunks and returns only completed rows; `finish()` returns the final in-progress row or `None` and resets for reuse.\n- Required behavior: LF/CRLF/lone CR record ends; CRLF split across chunks is one record end; quoted fields may contain delimiters and newlines; doubled quote is one literal quote; quote in unquoted field is ordinary; blank line produces no row; trailing record without newline is returned by `finish()`; `'a,'` yields `['a', '']`; char after closing quote other than delimiter/record end raises `ValueError` from `feed` or `finish`; `finish()` raises `ValueError` if a quoted field is still open.\n- Implemented design: states `_START`, `_FIELD`, `_QUOTED`, `_AFTER`; `_pending_cr` flag handles CR outside quotes so LF can form one CRLF end or CR can form a lone end; CR/LF inside `_QUOTED` are literal; `_AFTER` treats `\"` as doubled quote, delimiter as field commit, newline as record end, anything else as `ValueError`.\n- Parser rejects malformed doubled-quote sequences such as `\"\"b\"` because after the second quote the next char is not another quote, delimiter, or record end.\n- First test run: `python3 -m pytest -q` in the worktree produced `...........F......F.F..` with 3 failures:\n  - `test_garbage_after_closing_quote_raises`: parser raised during `s.feed('\"a\" ')`, but test expected the raise at `finish()`.\n  - `test_quote_pair_split_across_chunks`: original test data concatenated to malformed CSV, e.g. `a,\"\"b\"\\n`.\n  - `test_split_invariance_random_splits`: original data contained `\"t\"\"\\n`, which leaves the quoted field unterminated; a quoted field ending in a literal quote needs `\"t\"\"\"`.\n- Test fixes already applied to `tests/test_csvstream.py`:\n  - `test_garbage_after_closing_quote_raises` now expects `ValueError` during `s.feed('\"a\" ')`.\n  - `test_quote_pair_split_across_chunks` now uses valid split cases:\n    - `parse('a,\"x\"', '\"y\"\\n') == [['a', 'x\"y']]`\n    - `parse('a,\"x', '\"\"y\"\\n') == [['a', 'x\"y']]`\n    - `parse('a,\"x\"\"', '\"y\"\\n') == [['a', 'x\"\"y']]`\n  - `test_split_invariance_random_splits` data changed to:\n    - `'a,\"b,c\",d\\n\"x\"\"y\",\\r\\n\"q\\r\\nr\",s\\n\"t\"\"\"\\n\\nt,u'`\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repo structure and git state; confirmed branch `crew/1107-f186a4`, clean tree, and base commit `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Confirmed `ledgerkit/__init__.py` is empty and needs no export changes.\n- Created `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/csvstream.py` with the `CsvStream` state machine.\n- Created `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_csvstream.py` with the full planned test suite.\n- Ran initial `python3 -m pytest -q` and identified 3 test-data bugs, not parser bugs.\n- Applied 3 targeted edits to `tests/test_csvstream.py` to fix malformed test expectations/data.\n\n### Active\n- Need to rerun the test suite after the test-file edits to verify all tests pass.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` with workdir `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4` and verify all tests pass.\n2. If green, commit `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` and `tests/test_csvstream.py` to `crew/1107-f186a4` with a clear message, do not push, and report the exact pytest command and output.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/csvstream.py`: created; contains `CsvStream` streaming CSV parser.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_csvstream.py`: created and edited; contains tests for `CsvStream`, including split-invariance, CR/CRLF handling, quoted fields, errors, and reuse.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: verified empty; no changes needed.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/tests/test_money.py`: existing test used for import/style convention.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-f186a4/README.md`: documents test command `python3 -m pytest -q`.","time":{"start":1794049869843,"end":1794049888348}}}
